 "assistant_text": "Two failure stories to test—not forecasts—focus on customer losses and starter uptake.\n\n1. It is a year later and this decision went badly because ‘Raise prices 10%’ increased ‘Price rise from current price’, but ‘Customers lost from price rise’ eroded the revenue gain.\n   Watch for: Cancellation requests rose after customers received renewal notices.\n   Mitigate: Test the increase with a small renewal cohort before extending it.\n\n2. It is a year later and this decision went badly because ‘Launch starter tier’ set ‘Starter tier launched’, but weak starter uptake left monthly recurring revenue short of the goal.\n   Watch for: Starter sign-ups fell below your stated uptake range.\n   Mitigate: Test demand with a limited launch before committing more resources.\n\nOutside the model: Could existing customers have downgraded to the starter tier rather than it attracting only new subscribers?\n"
